## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The junction was busy for the entire hour with no quiet phase. Minutes 0–24 carried continuously heavy but moving mixed traffic with a steady stream of identifiable cars, buses, trucks and two-wheelers. From minute 25 conditions deteriorated into severe, near-gridlocked congestion that persisted through minute 55, with queues, stationary buses, filtering motorcyclists, high auto-rickshaw density and pedestrians threading between vehicles. From minute 56 flow resumed toward the camera. Dominant traffic throughout was private cars (white most common), two-wheelers and green-and-yellow auto-rickshaws, with a recurring mix of goods vehicles and buses. Recurrent elements: the red tractor with tanker trailer (mins 12, 32, 42), the red open-top off-road vehicle (mins 20, 42–45), the red city bus (mins 26, 43–45), the "PREMIUM EDIBLE OILS" truck (mins 40, 42), damp road surface after rain (mins 13, 19, 46), and repeated pedestrian incursions into the carriageway. The appearance of police vehicles at mins 49 and 59 coincided with the worst congestion and its easing.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None observed. Traffic was heavy or gridlocked for the full 60 minutes.
