# POLICE SUMMARY — CCTV cam14_stream-14 (Unknown Location, "DELIGHT P1 RLVD" junction)

**Footage:** 720 minutes (minutes 0–719), continuous, from Saturday 13-06-2026 evening through Sunday 14-06-2026 morning (~21:25 to ~08:15 by internal timestamps).

---

## 1. SCENE

The camera overlooks a large, signalised urban intersection in an Indian city (Delhi-style junction; CTU/DTC-style buses, GSRTC and "DELHI" coaches noted). The camera overlay "DELIGHT P1 RLVD" indicates a red-light-violation enforcement camera. A Coca-Cola branded kiosk/sign sits near the centre island (minutes 240, 488, 499); "WESTBANK" shops and a right-side hoarding/bus shelter line the right footpath. The footage is entirely night-time or pre-dawn until roughly minute 550, after which dull, hazy overcast early-morning daylight prevails. The road surface was repeatedly wet/reflective, indicating recent or ongoing rain, in many stretches (e.g. minutes 15, 21, 23, 29–32, 50–51, 58, 67, 77, 81, 84, 92, 96, 106, 109, 118, 120, 155–157, 162, 164–166, 169, 171, 173–174, throughout 225–249, from ~281 onward, 303, 307, 316, 318, 357, 360, 362, from ~395, and damp roads in the morning hours). Heavy headlight glare and motion blur limited detail throughout the dark hours.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE

Traffic was continuous mixed traffic at a signalised junction for the full 12 hours, free-flowing throughout with no jams.

- **Motorcycles/scooters:** present in every part; roughly 15–25 per minute at night peak (minutes 175–224), 8–20 per minute in the early hours, 6–15 overnight, rising again to 8–20 per minute after dawn. Many carried pillion riders (occasionally three riders, minute 281); many riders appeared helmetless, especially from minute 200 onward.
- **Auto-rickshaws:** a constant feature in every minute — early on in white, yellow, green, yellow-green, red, black and blue liveries; from roughly minute 175 onward overwhelmingly yellow-and-green CNG autos, typically 4–12 per minute, plus blue three-wheeler goods carriers and cycle-rickshaws.
- **Cars:** predominantly white hatchbacks, sedans, SUVs and MPVs, with recurring black/dark, silver/grey, red/maroon and occasional blue, gold/tan, lime-green and brown/orange vehicles. A recurring white hatchback entered from the left and exited right at ~30s in nearly every minute across the whole footage.
- **Buses:** frequent throughout — red, red/orange, blue, blue-and-white, white, orange/white, cream and double-decker city and intercity coaches; named/lettered buses included "GSRTC" (minute 36), "Model Patel" (minute 161), "AMER" (minute 287), "JALARAM" (minute 578), "SALUJA BUS SERVICE" (minute 582), "PUNJAB" (minute 605), "TANNA"/"ANNA" (minute 616), "SAI" (minute 644), "JAMIA" (minute 363), "HUMAN" (minute 690), "GURUDEV/GUILDFORD TRAVELS" (minute 684), "A.S" (minutes 710–711, 717), destination "401 Chandni" (minute 620).
- **Goods vehicles/trucks:** tarpaulin-covered goods trucks, tippers, concrete mixers, box trucks, tankers, a garbage truck (minute 125, and green refuse trucks minutes 286–287, 412, 582), a road-roller (minute 581), tractor-trolleys, road-sweeping machines, and branded trucks "BALA JI …JAIPUR" (minute 626), "ON DUTY" (minute 629), "AMC 15" (minute 631), "R.K.M. LOGISTICS" (minute 647).
- **Vans/emergency-type vehicles:** white vans including "FS COURIERS & CARGO SERVICE" (minute 85), "Ban…" branding (minute 46), ambulance-type vans with beacons (minutes 175, 183, 207, 210, 240, 277, 345, 377–383, 439, 505, 525, 533, 552, 567, 569, 654, 681, 684), police-type vehicles with blue lights (minutes 206, 353, 462, 463, 466, 631), a fire tender (minute 269).
- **Pedestrians:** heavy footpath crowds at night (roughly 20–50 people on the right footpath near the lit shops, minutes 200–224; ~20–30 at minute 235; 6–10 loiterers at minute 249), thinning to sparse individuals and small groups (1–4) overnight and in the morning. Crossings were occasional and mostly at zebras; one person in bright orange/red clothing walked on the carriageway among traffic (minute 215). Cyclists and hand-carts appeared intermittently.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED

