## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION

No traffic jams or blockages occurred at any point; traffic was described as free-flowing in every part. Pedestrian crowd build-ups on footpaths: roughly 20–50 people on the right footpath near the lit shops through minutes 200–224; crowds of ~20–30 at minute 235; 6–10 loiterers near white barricades at minute 249; standing groups of 3–8 near the right-side hoarding/bus shelter through minutes 250–268. Vehicle queues at red signals: groups of up to 15–20 two-wheelers waiting (minutes 695, 699 area); queues of two-wheelers, autos, a dark sedan and a white mini-truck at stop lines (minutes 667, 669, 671); a large pale-roofed bus briefly blocked the view (minute 248); a large dark bus briefly blocked the view (minute 319); an orange/yellow bus occupied the near crossing for the whole of minute 692; a blue open-body tipper stopped centre-foreground (minutes 718–719); a green refuse truck stationary in the foreground (minutes 286–287); a red bus stationary bottom centre (minutes 3–4).

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS

- Minute 477 — white van/MPV stopped briefly on the zebra crossing.
- Minute 538 — multiple vehicles (a white car, a dark car and several autos) ran the red/amber signal.
- Minute 580 — near-side signal showing amber/red for much of the time yet largely unheeded by traffic.
- Minute 599 — apparent collision involving a white SUV (~14s).
- Minute 654 — ambulance with beacon apparently ran a red light.
- Helmetless riders: observed extensively from minute 200 onward (minutes 200–224 "many appearing unhelmeted"), minute 633, and by minute 673 "some helmetless"; few visible helmets also noted minutes 150–174.
- Minutes 254 onward — the "DELIGHT P1 RLVD" red-light-enforcement overlay was intermittently visible, indicating the camera operates in red-light-violation detection mode.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY

The footage covers a full 12-hour cycle at a busy signalised Delhi-style junction. The busiest period was Saturday night, roughly minutes 175–249 (approximately 23:15–01:30), when two-wheeler traffic reached 15–25 per minute and pedestrian crowds of 20–50 gathered on the right footpath outside the lit shops. Traffic then lightened steadily through the small hours: minutes 275–499 were consistently light overnight traffic dominated by two-wheelers and yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws, with goods vehicles (tippers, mixers, container trucks) and intercity coaches prominent — consistent with overnight freight movement. From roughly minute 500 (05:19) activity gradually built again with morning commuters, cyclists, cycle-rickshaws and pedestrians returning, though volumes remained "light-to-moderate" through to the end of the footage (~08:15). The dominant vehicle types across the entire period were motorcycles/scooters (frequently two-up, increasingly helmetless after midnight) and yellow-and-green CNG auto-rickshaws, present in every single minute. A white hatchback entering from the left and exiting right at ~30 seconds was a near-constant recurrence across all 720 minutes. City buses of many liveries passed throughout. Rain/wet roads recurred in waves (early evening, late evening, overnight and pre-dawn). Signal phases cycled normally; the near-side signal showed amber/red for much of the night with compliance appearing weaker in the early hours.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS

The quietest stretches, with consistently light traffic and virtually no pedestrian activity, were:

- Minutes 275–349 (approximately 01:54–03:49): consistently light, free-flowing overnight traffic; pedestrians rare to absent (from minute 269 onward no pedestrians on foot were observed for a stretch).
- Minutes 350–449 (approximately 02:49–04:49): light pre-dawn traffic, pedestrians rare (single individuals only; one clear pedestrian at minute 360, one at minute 411).
- Minutes 450–499 (approximately 04:50–05:18): very light pre-dawn traffic; pedestrians rare and isolated.

No minute in the entire footage was completely devoid of traffic; even the quietest periods carried a steady flow of two-wheelers and auto-rickshaws.
